  "articleBody": "Log cabins are beautiful, but they need regular maintenance to stay that way, especially with Colorado's weather. One of the most critical tasks is restaining. But how do you know when it's time? There are several tell-tale signs to look out for. First, if you notice your logs are starting to gray or look faded, that's a big indicator. The stain protects the wood from UV rays, and once it starts to break down, the wood beneath becomes vulnerable. Another sign is checking for peeling, flaking, or cracking stain. This means the existing finish is failing and no longer providing adequate protection. You might also notice moisture absorption; if water soaks into the logs instead of beading up on the surface, the stain's waterproofing capabilities are gone. Finally, if you see mold, mildew, or insect activity, a failing stain could be part of the problem. Don't let these issues go unaddressed; they can lead to more serious and costly damage down the line. HH Remodeling LLC, with Abraham Becerra's expertise, offers professional log and cabin refinishing services across our wide service area, from Boulder to Colorado Springs. Getting a fresh restain not only restores your cabin's beauty but also extends its life and protects your investment. If you're seeing any of these signs, it's definitely time to reach out to a professional.",
